{"type":"text","timestamp":1794305332078,"sessionID":"ses_e3b11b142ffehyUsg0hi8c2GGs","part":{"id":"prt_1c4ee9338001b0Bgl6pn6iI9KT","messageID":"msg_1c4ee7c2b001WDfm0c0d8uuRxT","sessionID":"ses_e3b11b142ffehyUsg0hi8c2GGs","type":"text","text":"<think>Let me check the environment: python version, node version, available packages, network access to package registries.\n\nLet me plan:\n1. Backend: Flask app with SQLite storage under `./data`. Auth with tokens (bearer). Password hashing (use hashlib pbkdf2 from stdlib to avoid extra dependency - werkzeug has generate_password_hash built in! Werkzeug is a Flask dependency, so `werkzeug.security` is available). Token: use `itsdangerous` (Flask dep) to sign tokens, or just store tokens in DB. Simpler: use itsdangerous URLSafeTimedSerializer with a secret key. But secret key needs to persist across restarts — store in data dir or env var. Let's generate and store in ./data/secret.key.\n\n2. Frontend: React + TS + Vite + Tailwind. Need tailwind v4 probably (with @tailwindcss/vite plugin). Need to add dependency to package.json and update lockfile. npm install with network access — sandbox can install packages from public registries through a read-only cache. Let me test.\n\nLet me check what tooling is available.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794305332024,"end":1794305332071}}}
