{"type":"text","timestamp":1794305376356,"sessionID":"ses_e3b11b142ffehyUsg0hi8c2GGs","part":{"id":"prt_1c4ef404f001JtB76mL7oG8KGw","messageID":"msg_1c4ef2f3f001oet5NuqaTCSGRp","sessionID":"ses_e3b11b142ffehyUsg0hi8c2GGs","type":"text","text":"<think>Hmm, the mkdir -p /tmp/opencode/piptest fails? Odd. Maybe the issue was the `mkdir -p` combined with pip in one command being flagged. Let me just try pip install into a venv in /workspace or use pip install --target. Actually let me try pip install with a venv inside /tmp/opencode.\n\nActually the error might be caused by the combined command. Let me try separately.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794305376335,"end":1794305376352}}}
