{"type":"text","timestamp":1794305570565,"sessionID":"ses_e3b11b142ffehyUsg0hi8c2GGs","part":{"id":"prt_1c4f236f8001oJ17Q4gebrYlWr","messageID":"msg_1c4f22bb20012rl63vN1NFrNiE","sessionID":"ses_e3b11b142ffehyUsg0hi8c2GGs","type":"text","text":"<think>Hmm, \"avoid hand-written CSS files except for Tailwind's own entry file\" — index.css IS Tailwind's entry file, so `@import \"tailwindcss\";` is fine. The @theme block is Tailwind config within the entry file — acceptable. The `html { color-scheme: light; }` is a small addition; maybe remove it to stay strictly within \"Tailwind's own entry file\" utilities. I can use `class=\"scheme-light\"` on the html element in index.html instead. Let me remove the custom CSS rule and use the utility class in index.html.\n\nLet me rewrite index.css minimal.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794305570552,"end":1794305570562}}}
