{"type":"text","timestamp":1794305587453,"sessionID":"ses_e3b11b142ffehyUsg0hi8c2GGs","part":{"id":"prt_1c4f278f0001ibad4KhAPOx0uG","messageID":"msg_1c4f264e0001oZYSUvHWSSnKf3","sessionID":"ses_e3b11b142ffehyUsg0hi8c2GGs","type":"text","text":"<think>Note: `React.ReactNode` used without importing React — with `jsx: react-jsx` and `verbatimModuleSyntax`, the `React` namespace isn't automatically available as a value but as a type it needs `import type { ReactNode } from \"react\"`. Let me use `import type { ReactNode } from \"react\";` and `children: ReactNode`.\n\nLet me fix that in router.tsx.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794305587441,"end":1794305587450}}}
